<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60292" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρώβυλ-ος</span></b>  (parox., v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.163
		</span></i>), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>roll</i> or <i>knot of hair on the crown of the
			head</i>, worn at Athens, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρωβύλον ἀναδούμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				189
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				980
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> nickname of
			the orator Hegesippus, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.118
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> name of a
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορνοβοσκός</span>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρωβύλου ζεῦγος</span> 'a precious pair',
				<i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				91.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>tuft of hair</i> on a helmet, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.4.13
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
